"Arrival Station F, also called the Teleportation Complex, is F City's teleport travel center."
"A long hallway there is lined with phonebooth-sized teleportation bays."
"Each bay has an arched ceiling covered in spiraling symbols and a door like a blank metal wall."
"A female voice in each bay asks arrivals to submit to a scan or wait for an in-person check."
"Lit WAY OUT signs in five languages lead from the bays to a wide atrium of potted palms."
"The atrium help desk issues NesiCard debit cards after a thumbprint check."
"Post Drop #1301, a talking mailbox nicknamed Leo, is by the station's exit."
"Departures run in time slots, through a departures lounge and security scanners."
"Bays monitor arrivals' vital signs by camera and sensor while security decides to release them."
"Avowed back from long stays on the Triplanets are held until a therapist screens them."
"The complex has automatic doors, a local arrivals hall and a Jamaican food spot in the atrium."
"Loud toilet-flush sounds near the Post Drop come from Leo getting in the zone."
"The complex has bike racks, shops and restaurants, and a customer service desk."
"Artonans helped build the complex, 'an enormous, well-dressed summonarium', to ease the System."
"Capsized boaters and Avowed in trouble can emergency-teleport themselves to the complex."
"Pets are scanned for diseases and magical contraband and tagged before teleporting out."
"Its bright, clean parking garage is painted with colorful murals."
"The whole building is a teleporter, with magic symbols hidden under its floor tiles."
"Its full capacity is only for use if Anesidora is no longer a suitable place to live."
"In the Matadero crisis the System dropped hundreds of children at once into its concourse."
"Heavy use frosts its magic symbols with ice, which workers chip off, and cracks tiles."
"A hangar holds an Artonan escape shuttle, with a comfort-toy cubby for children."
"A warming room shelters Avowed on emergency orders between rescue tasks."
"It runs scheduled batch teleports, such as one at 7:45 p.m., and has aerial vehicle parking."
"Its teleshipping area handles freight; a larger entrance can take 'a bus through sideways'."
"Post Drop #1301 by the exit sings adverts, and seems oddly fragile to Alden's targeting sense."
